+### Turning Wiki Reads Off
+
+To stop agents from reading the wiki (to seed or inform their context) while still letting them propose wiki changes, add this to `.ta/workflow.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[wiki]
+seed_context = false
+```
+
+With `seed_context = false` the TA gateway refuses `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types`, for goal agents and for chat-mode Chief-of-Staff sessions alike. The refusal names the setting and the file and tells you how to turn reads back on. `ta_wiki_create`, `ta_wiki_update` and the draft-review write path keep working as before.
+
+The default is `true`, so a project with no `[wiki]` section behaves as it always did. `ta doctor` prints a `wiki reads` line when the switch is off, so you can see why reads are refused. A value that is not `true` or `false` makes reads fail closed with an error naming `.ta/workflow.toml` and `seed_context`.
+
 ### Wiki Writes Are Reviewed
 
 `ta_wiki_create` and `ta_wiki_update` do not write to the wiki when an agent calls them. They check the input and queue the change in the goal's draft. Nothing reaches Wayfinder until you approve and apply that draft. `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types` are unchanged and read live.
